<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.2.1: Squares in a Geometric Pattern</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01757</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.2.1: Squares in a Geometric Pattern</md:title>
    <md:uuid>77ebfb2c-574f-4ae3-9734-cbd1fd8204a4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>How does each expression represent the number of small squares in the figure?</para>
<para><figure><media alt="An image of a block of squares. There are eight squares on rows 1, 2, 3 and 4 and five squares on rows 5 - 6. There are six squares missing from the upper right corner of the block."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5b2f937385dd355382040846e4eb54b535d7ba6b"/></media></figure></para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Expression A: \(6 \cdot 8−2 \cdot 3\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>There are 6 rows with 8 small squares, but from this, 2 rows of 3 small squares have been removed.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Expression B: \(4 \cdot 8+2 \cdot 5\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>There are 4 rows of 8 small squares, and to this, 2 rows of 5 small squares are added.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Expression C: \(8+8+8+8+5+5\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>This counts each row, starting from the bottom.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Expression D: \(5 \cdot 6+3 \cdot 4\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>There are 5 columns of 6 small squares and 3 columns of 4 small squares.</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Interaction End -->
<div class="os-raise-student-reflection">
  <para class="os-raise-student-reflection-title">Building Character: Proactivity</para>
  <div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-gap-1">
    <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2aad4f3d5b5d9c496973ad6f7a2e199296b9b776"/></media></figure><div>
      <para class="os-raise-mb-0">Proactivity is the ability to take initiative. There’s evidence that proactivity is one of the qualities that distinguished the greatest American presidents from their peers. </para>
      <para>Think about your current sense of proactivity. Are the following statements are true for you?</para>
      <list>
        <item>
          I am always looking for better ways of doing things.
        </item>
        <item>
          I love to challenge the status quo. 
        </item>
      </list>
      <para>Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
     </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
</content>
